Values University Profile Consumer Information College Auxiliary Services Campus Facilities Directions & Campus Maps MyPlattsburgh Make a Gift Who are you? Current Students Parents & Families School Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Community Jump to Footer Helping You Move From Now to Next Your career center helps synthesize your education and experiences as you prepare\n                              for life after college. From career exploration to resumes to job search to grad school,\n                              we have the tools and expertise to empower you toward a meaningful professional life. Helping You Move From Now to Next Your career center helps synthesize your education and experiences as you prepare\n                              for life after college. From career exploration to resumes to job search to grad school,\n                              we have the tools and expertise to empower you toward a meaningful professional life. Visit Us Visit Apply Now Apply Request Info Info Go back to the SUNY Plattsburgh Home Page PlattsLife Career Development Center Career Development Center Your Career Center — From Day One Career development is a process that takes time. Meet with us early in your college\n                                 experience, virtually or in person. We will help you build a plan for your college\n                                 years that includes much more than a diploma. 30K+ Active job & internship postings How Students Get Hired Check out available jobs and internships on Handshake. Login to Handshake Our Pledge To You The mission of the Career Development Center is to educate and empower students toward\n                           meaningful careers and life-long professional success, engaging the campus, alumni,\n                           and employer communities as our partners. Let’s Get Started Personal Career Coaching for Students & Alumni The CDC is available to students and alumni for all career coaching needs. We offer\n                                          individual appointments with our counselors virtually and in person on a range of\n                                          topics, including: Resume and cover letter review and development Job/internship searching Career exploration Choosing a major Graduate school Interview preparation Make an Appointment Career Closet Our Career Closet features gently used clothing for interviews, internships, conferences\n                                          and other events that require professional dress. Items are free to students. Call\n                                          or stop by the Career Development Center for more information. Monday – Friday from 8 a.m. – 4 p.m. We are located in 118 Angell College Center LinkedIn Headshot Photos LinkedIn Headshots LinkedIn is a powerful platform used for career exploration, networking, and job searching.\n                                          It is important to have a complete profile, including a photo. The Career Development\n                                          Center offers free headshots! Simply make an appointment . Wear a nice top or shirt, and come see us! Hours of availability are from 9 a.m. – 4 p.m. Monday through Friday. Career Exploration & Assessments The Career Development Center offers opportunities virtually and in person to explore\n                                          career options with a career counselor. During these sessions you may be offered the\n                                          opportunity to take an assessment which can further assist in exploring different\n                                          careers Make A Career Exploration Appointment Job & Internship Search Strategy The Career Development Center offers virtual and in-person appointments to assist\n                                          you in developing your job and/or internship search strategy. Schedule an appointment\n                                          with us to get started. Make a Job/Internship Search Appointment Special Events Annually, the Career Development Center offers a career fair, graduate and professional\n                                          school fair, etiquette dinners, workshops, and more. Be sure to check out our latest\n                                          events. Upcoming Events How We Help You Get Career Ready How your college experience can help you be career ready: Academic group projects and research experience: Develop communication, critical thinking, teamwork and technology skills. Student activities, clubs and athletics: Build leadership and exposure to different perspectives helping develop equity and\n                                          inclusion skills. Working a part-time job and internships: Develop professionalism and technology skills, while furthering your career and self-development. Here is what employers want you to have experience with before your graduate: Career and self-development Communication Critical thinking Equity and inclusion Leadership Professionalism Teamwork Technology Work with us, and we can help you be career ready! Resources for Alumni Welcome back! We are excited that you are interested in connecting with the SUNY Plattsburgh\n                                          Career Development Center (CDC). If you are a recent graduate, be sure to log into Handshake to complete your First Destination Survey. Post a job/internship — Please visit our Employers page for information on how to get your job or internship opportunity in front of current\n                                             Plattsburgh students. Career Consultation — Schedule a virtual or in-person appointment, and we can assist you with your resume, job search, interviewing, salary expectations,\n                                             and more. Handshake — An online comprehensive career management portal with job postings, resume help,\n                                             and more. Volunteer/mentor — If you want to volunteer or mentor to help a current student with career issues,\n                                             we welcome your involvement. Opportunities to serve include: guest speaker, resume\n                                             reviewer, practice interviewer, job shadow host, or career mentor. Email us so we\n                                             can find out how you can reconnect with SUNY Plattsburgh. Please also visit your alumni website to discover all the ways you can connect with Cardinals! Career Development Center Connect with a Career Counselor Events Career Tools Job & Internship Postings On-Campus Student Employment Internships & Grants Parents & Families Prospective Employers Faculty First Destination Survey Staff Directory Contact Us Career Development Center 118 Angell College Center 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-2071 Fax: 518-564-5080 [email protected] Like us on Facebook. Follow us on Twitter. Follow us on Instagram. Career Development Center Connect with a Career Counselor Events Career Tools Job & Internship Postings On-Campus Student Employment Internships & Grants Parents & Families Prospective Employers Faculty First Destination Survey Staff Directory Contact Us Career Development Center 118 Angell College Center 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-2071 Fax: 518-564-5080 [email protected] Like us on Facebook. Follow us on Twitter. Follow us on Instagram. News Alumni Association Bestows Leadership Professional, Emerita Lecturer with Impact Awards September 8, 2026 Students Engage with Clubs, Organizations at SUNY Plattsburgh Involvement Fair September 4, 2026 Heller-Ross Achieves SUNY’s Highest Rank of Distinguished Librarian September 3, 2026 Plattsburgh in the News BHSN to host CIT training The Sun PLATTSBURGH | Behavioral Health Services North's (BHSN) Mobile Crisis Team and SUNY\n                                 Plattsburgh... Shelter Islander on the brink of American Ninja Warrior finals - Shelter Island Reporter Shelter Island Reporter That young man you see flying through the air with the greatest of ease is 23-year-old\n                                 Luke... View All News View All Events Jump to Header Plattsburgh State University of New York Like us on Facebook. Find us on Instagram. Connect with us on Snapchat. Connect with us on LinkedIn. Login required. Watch us on YouTube. Virtual Tour Employment Emergency Info Find People Consumer Info Accessibility Title IX Feinberg Library Bookstore 101 Broad Street , Plattsburgh, NY 12901 • 518-564-2000 Copyright © 1996 – Privacy Policy Contact Us Last Updated 8/31/26 Back to top"
    },
