Values University Profile Consumer Information College Auxiliary Services Campus Facilities Directions & Campus Maps MyPlattsburgh Make a Gift Who are you? Current Students Parents & Families School Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Community Jump to Footer Go back to the SUNY Plattsburgh Home Page Cost & Aid Work-Study & Student Jobs Work-Study & Student Jobs There are many opportunities available if you wish to work while in college. 500+ 500+ Part-Time Jobs Sign in to Handshake SUNY Plattsburgh students work on campus each year The Part-Time Job Fest showcases on- and off-campus job opportunities available with\n                                             a variety of employers. Sign in to Handshake Types of Student Employment You can find work on-campus through the federal work-study program or student temporary\n                           service. Local businesses and organizations also support our students with part-time\n                           job opportunities. Participation in the community advocate program is another way\n                           to help reduce your college costs. For graduate students, assistantship programs are\n                           available to eligible students to assist with educational expenses. Work-study is a federal student aid program that provides part-time employment. Students who\n                              file the FAFSA closest to October 1 each year, select interest in work-study on the\n                              FAFSA, and demonstrate financial need may be awarded. Wages earned from participation\n                              in the program helps students with monthly educational and personal expenses, but\n                              are not deducted from the college bill. The current wage rate for most work-study\n                              jobs is $15.50/hour. Temporary service offers part-time student jobs in various departments across campus. Like work-study,\n                              wages earned from temp service helps students with monthly educational and personal\n                              expenses, but are not deducted from the college bill. The current wage rate for most\n                              temp service jobs is $15.50/hour. Off-campus jobs may be available in professional offices, restaurants, retail establishments and\n                              other local businesses. Area residents also hire students for help with childcare,\n                              yardwork or housework. Community advocate (CA) positions help reduce students housing and board costs, in return for building community by\n                              providing programming, floor meetings and assistance with residence hall safety and\n                              security. Visit Campus Housing and Community Living to learn more about becoming a CA. Graduate assistantships are available in housing, administrative and academic areas on campus. Funding supplied\n                              to graduate assistants comes in the form of tuition scholarships and direct stipends.\n                              Learn more about SUNY Plattsburgh’s graduate assistantships . Experience Opportunities at SUNY Plattsburgh Make the most of your SUNY Plattsburgh experience. Involvement in student employment,\n                           internships and assistantships helps defray college costs while building skills relevant\n                           to your future. Financial Aid Handshake Career Portal Career Development Graduate Students Cost & Aid Apply for Aid Net Price Calculator Tuition & Fees Scholarships, Loans & Grants Work-Study & Student Jobs Federal Stimulus Grants Bill Payment, Refunds & Payment Plans Financial Services Forms Financial Aid Resources for Graduate Students Special Circumstance Student Loan Code of Conduct Current Student Aid Staff Contact Us Student Financial Services 401–405 Kehoe Administration Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-2072 Toll Free: 877-768-5976 Fax: 518-564-4079 [email protected] Hours Monday – Friday 8 a.m to 4 p.m. (Thursdays 9 a.m. to 4 p.m.) Visit Us Visit Apply Now Apply Request Info Info Cost & Aid Apply for Aid Net Price Calculator Tuition & Fees Scholarships, Loans & Grants Work-Study & Student Jobs Federal Stimulus Grants Bill Payment, Refunds & Payment Plans Financial Services Forms Financial Aid Resources for Graduate Students Special Circumstance Student Loan Code of Conduct Current Student Aid Staff Contact Us Student Financial Services 401–405 Kehoe Administration Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-2072 Toll Free: 877-768-5976 Fax: 518-564-4079 [email protected] Hours Monday – Friday 8 a.m to 4 p.m. (Thursdays 9 a.m. to 4 p.m.) Visit Us Visit Apply Now Apply Request Info Info Jump to Header Plattsburgh State University of New York Like us on Facebook. Find us on Instagram. Connect with us on Snapchat. Connect with us on LinkedIn. Login required. Watch us on YouTube. Virtual Tour Employment Emergency Info Find People Consumer Info Accessibility Title IX Feinberg Library Bookstore 101 Broad Street , Plattsburgh, NY 12901 • 518-564-2000 Copyright © 1996 – Privacy Policy Contact Us Last Updated 8/31/26 Back to top"
