    "https://jobs.plattsburgh.edu/postings/search": {
      "title": "Search  ATRs(76)",
      "description": "SUNY College at Plattsburgh Employment Site | Search Jobs Skip to Main Content SUNY Plattsburgh > Human Resources Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Notice of Non-Discrimination Pay Equity Executive Order Return to Human Resources Services Search  ATRs (76) Hide Search Options To view open positions, please enter your search criteria below.  You may view all open positions by not specifying any search criteria and clicking the Search button. Keywords Posted Within Any time period Last Day Last Week Last Month Job Category No Selection Clerical/Maintenance/Service Academic Professional Librarian Graduate Assistant Part-Time Faculty Go to search results page: Previous 1 2 3 Next (76) To view the position details and/or apply to an open position, click on the position title or the View Details link.  If you would like to bookmark a position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. Student Financial Services Counselor This position will be responsible for phone, email, virtual and in-person financial advising; aid program management; financial transactions; and promoting cost and aid awareness through on campus presentations and student facing events. Student Financial Services (SFS) provides accessible, accurate, and responsive financial aid and student account services that enable students to successfully ... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Communication Studies Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching in an institution dedicated primarily to undergraduate education. They will be expected to demonstrate an understanding of and sensitivity to diversity and gender issues, as SUNY Plattsburgh is committed to ensuring that its graduates are educated to succeed in an increasingly complex, multicultural, and interdependent world.The ... View Details Bookmark Admissions Assistant As part of a dynamic Office of Undergraduate Admissions team, this position plays a key role in recruiting, converting, and enrolling academically qualified undergraduate students at SUNY Plattsburgh. The successful candidate will contribute to a comprehensive enrollment strategy through a combination of recruitment, outreach, and application review activities. Primary responsibilities include,... View Details Bookmark Contract Associate The Contract Associate provides professional administrative, procurement, and contract management support for the University’s capital construction program. This role coordinates procurement and contract administration activities for capital improvement projects funded through the State University Construction Fund (SUCF), the Dormitory Authority of the State of New York (DASNY), and other capi... View Details Bookmark Athletic Facilities & Operations Assistant This position will be primarily responsible for providing operational assistance to the athletic department and the field house complex. This will include athletic facility scheduling, working with outside groups on permit and rental processes, serving as a point of contact for large-scale campus events, managing ticketing for athletic events, supervising student workers, and assisting the Assi... View Details Bookmark Maintenance Assistant Join our Maintenance Trades team and play an important role in keeping our campus facilities safe, functional, and well maintained. As a Maintenance Assistant, you will be responsible for processing all work order requests received, and handling them accurately and timely.The Maintenance Trades department is part of the Administration & Finance Division, which provides essential services to... View Details Bookmark Trades Specialist (Electrician)/Trainee Join our Maintenance Trades team and play an important role in keeping our campus facilities safe, functional, and well maintained. As an Electrician you will perform journeyman electrician work and frequently supervise others in repair, maintenance, and installation of electrical systems and equipment. The electrical trade, for reasons of safety, requires care and precision in its performance ... View Details Bookmark Access Control Technician - Enterprise Systems & Solutions We are seeking a motivated technologist to join our team to assist with the administration, support, documentation, and improvement of campus access control and video surveillance systems as part of the Enterprise Systems & Solutions team, a unit within Information Technology Services (ITS). This position will support the Lenel OnGuard access control system, the Milestone video management s... View Details Bookmark Inspector, University Police The Inspector conducts, supervises, and manages investigations of campus-related criminal misconduct and/or violations of campus policy. Responsibilities include the oversight of complete, accurate, and thorough investigations that occur utilizing current technology, recognized best practices, proper evidence collection, analysis, security, storage, and disposal, to ensure case integrity and vi... View Details Bookmark Facility Operations Assistant 1 Join the Janitorial team within our Facilities, Maintenance & Operations department to provide assistance to various crews, including janitorial, grounds, moving crew, and maintenance and operations. As a Facility Operations Assistant 1, you will perform a variety of tasks to help keep our campus facilities safe, functional, and well maintained.The Janitorial department is part of the Admin... View Details Bookmark Assistant College Registrar The Office of the Registrar seeks a detail oriented and tech savvy individual to join their dynamic staff. This full-time, 12-month position will perform various registrar functions, including but not limited to: assisting with course schedule production and training department personnel; processing student requests for registration at other campuses; maintaining accurate information in the mas... View Details Bookmark Office Assistant 1 (NY HELPS) This position supports the Facilities, Maintenance & Operations department by coordinating, processing, and dispatching work order requests accurately and promptly. The department provides campus-wide planning, construction, maintenance, and facility improvement services to support the University’s operations and educational mission. As part of the Administration and Finance Division, the p... View Details Bookmark Grounds Worker - Facility Operations Assistant 1 (Grounds) (Multiple Positions) Grounds Maintenance is dedicated to maintaining the natural beauty of our 265-acre campus completing routine maintenance for a variety of surfaces and areas. We are part of the Administration & Finance division and provide essential services to our campus, local, state, federal and international customers. We navigate systems in a collaborative and sensitive way to assist the University in ... View Details Bookmark Senior Advancement Officer We are seeking a results-driven Senior Advancement Officer who will play a key role in increasing charitable support for the university by identifying, qualifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding major, leadership, and planned gift donors. This position is responsible for expanding the university’s major gift pipeline and building meaningful philanthropic relationships that advance inst... View Details Bookmark Cleaner (Part-Time) - Temporary Janitorial Services is dedicated to maintaining a safe, healthy, and inviting learning, living and working environment for our campus community. We are part of the Administration & Finance division which provides essential services to our campus, local, state, federal and international customers. We are responsible for human, physical, financial and technical resources. As professionals, we... View Details Bookmark Cleaner (Temporary) Janitorial Services is dedicated to maintaining a safe, healthy, and inviting learning, living and working environment for our college community. We are part of the Administration & Finance division which provides essential services to our campus, local, state, federal and international customers. We are responsible for human, physical, financial and technical resources. As professionals, w... View Details Bookmark Academic Affairs Initiatives Coordinator The Academic Affairs Initiatives Coordinator will support the implementation of strategic priorities and initiatives across Academic Affairs at SUNY Plattsburgh. Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Academic Affairs, this position will collaborate with academic departments, administrative offices, and SUNY partners to advance institutional goals through project coordination, process im... View Details Bookmark Temporary Lecturer, Social Work (3 positions) Expected to begin in Fall 2026 and last for one year, with the possibility of a one year renewal, we are seeking skilled social work educators who will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and graduate courses across the Social Work Program curriculum depending on departmental needs and the candidates’ expertise. Responsibilities will include teaching 12 credits (4 courses) each semester a... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Political Science The Political Science Department of the State University of New York College at Plattsburgh is seeking qualified individuals to teach courses on a part-time, as needed basis. Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching in an institution dedicated primarily to undergraduate education. They will be expected to demonstrate an understanding of and sensitivity to diversity and ... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Assistant Librarian-Instruction The Feinberg Library seeks part-time, temporary instructors to teach sections of a one-credit course in Information & Technology Literacy.Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching in an institution dedicated primarily to undergraduate education. As SUNY Plattsburgh is an institution that delivers challenging and high-quality educational experiences to a diverse group... View Details Bookmark Assistant Coach (Part-Time) SUNY Plattsburgh’s department of Athletics & Recreation seeks qualified candidates to serve in part-time assistant coaching positions for the following sports; baseball, men’s basketball, women’s basketball, men’s lacrosse, women’s lacrosse, men’s soccer, women’s soccer, softball, and women’s volleyball. The successful candidates will assist each sport’s head coach in all aspects of managin... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Computer Science The Computer Science Department seeks applicants to teach courses in Computer Science, Computer Security and/or Information Technology at the SUNY Plattsburgh Branch at Queensbury which serves approximately 350 full and part-time students in undergraduate and graduate degree programs, as well as graduate students in certificate of advanced studies programs.The Computer Science Department works ... View Details Bookmark Part-Time Clinical Audiologist This position will provide basic diagnostics and aural rehabilitation/hearing aid dispensing for pediatrics and adults within the Speech & Hearing Center at SUNY Plattsburgh’s main campus. The Speech and Hearing Center serves as an academic facility for student clinicians and provides services to individuals with communication disorders and hearing loss. This position is expected to provide... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Physics The Physics Department at SUNY Plattsburgh is seeking qualified individuals to teach introductory Physics labs on a part-time basis.Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching in an institution dedicated primarily to undergraduate education. As SUNY Plattsburgh is an institution that delivers challenging and high-quality educational experiences to a diverse group of learne... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Counselor Education Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching in an institution dedicated primarily to undergraduate education. They will be expected to demonstrate an understanding of and sensitivity to diversity and gender issues, as SUNY Plattsburgh is committed to ensuring that its graduates are educated to succeed in an increasingly complex, multicultural, and interdependent world.The ... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Social Work Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching in an institution dedicated primarily to undergraduate education. They will be expected to demonstrate an understanding of and sensitivity to diversity and gender issues, as SUNY Plattsburgh is committed to ensuring that its graduates are educated to succeed in an increasingly complex, multicultural, and interdependent world.The ... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Exercise and Nutrition Sciences Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching in an institution dedicated primarily to undergraduate education. They will be expected to demonstrate an understanding of and sensitivity to diversity and gender issues, as SUNY Plattsburgh is committed to ensuring that its graduates are educated to succeed in an increasingly complex, multicultural, and interdependent world.Some... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Psychology Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching in an institution dedicated primarily to undergraduate education. They will be expected to demonstrate an understanding of and sensitivity to diversity and gender issues, as SUNY Plattsburgh is committed to ensuring that its graduates are educated to succeed in an increasingly complex, multicultural, and interdependent world.Some... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Education (all programs) The Education Department is committed to excellence in teaching, teacher preparation, and educational leadership preparation. Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching coursework dedicated to preparing undergraduate and graduate students in one or more of our Education programs, including childhood education, adolescence education, special education, and educational lead... View Details Bookmark Adjunct Faculty, Human Development and Family Relations (Queensbury Campus) Successful candidates will teach course(s) and collaborate with staff and faculty at the Plattsburgh main campus in the department of Human Development and Family Relations (HDFR). The HDFR Department prepares students to address issues that affect human living and development, and to work in various human services professions that support the wellbeing of individuals, families, and communities... View Details Bookmark Go to search results page: Previous 1 2 3 Next COPYRIGHT © 1996 - 2011 SUNY Plattsburgh • 101 Broad St. • Plattsburgh, NY 12901 • (518) 564-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.plattsburgh.edu/about/offices-divisions/academic-affairs/sponsored-research/prospective-employees.html": {
      "title": "Prospective Employees",
      "description": "Prospective Employees | SUNY Plattsburgh twitter brain business compass computer environment exit-site globe graph handshake health justice measure networking open-pdf pencil science trend video world arrow-right bars blogger caret-down caret-left caret-right caret-up close facebook gears home instagram linkedin logo play plus quote search snapchat-ghost tumblr virtual-tour women-network world-globe youtube-play logo-white Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Jump to Main Content Plattsburgh State University of New York Site Search Search Search SUNY Plattsburgh Visit Us Visit Apply Now Apply Request Info Info Academics Majors & Minors Online Programs Graduate Programs Microcredentials Schools & Departments Queensbury Campus Career Development Center Honors Program Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Academic Advising Feinberg Library Learning Center Study Abroad & Exchanges Technology Services Admissions First-Year Transfer Graduate International Readmission Educational Opportunity Program Non-Matriculated Students Registration Dates & Forms Apply Now Check Your Application Status Request More Information Visit & Event Options Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Scholarships, Loans & Grants Work Study & Student Jobs Apply for Aid Bill Paying & Refunds Net Price Calculator Graduate Student Aid Current Student Financial Aid Financial Services Forms PlattsLife Calendar of Events Activities & Getting Involved Campus Housing & Community Living Food & Dining Virtual Tour Our Location Visual & Performing Arts Campus TV & Radio Stations Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Health & Safety Career Development Center Student Support & Resources First Year Student Programs Commencement Sustainability Athletics Cardinal Athletics Recreational Sports & Programs Facilities Fitness Center Ticket Sales About Us President & Leadership Campus News Offices & Divisions Centers, Institutes & Clinics SUNY Plattsburgh at Queensbury Plattsburgh Next Mission, Vision & Values University Profile Consumer Information College Auxiliary Services Campus Facilities Directions & Campus Maps MyPlattsburgh Make a Gift Who are you? Current Students Parents & Families School Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Community Jump to Footer Go back to the SUNY Plattsburgh Home Page About SUNY Plattsburgh Offices & Divisions Academic Affairs Division Sponsored Research & Programs Prospective Employees Prospective Employees Employment opportunities offered by the Research Foundation for SUNY are separate\n                              and distinct from SUNY and State University of New York employment. Employment opportunities offered by the Research Foundation for SUNY are separate\n                           and distinct from SUNY and State University of New York employment. As a result, position\n                           terms and conditions, compensation and benefits offered by the Research Foundation\n                           are different from state employment. Contact the Research Foundation Human Resources\n                           office at SUNY Plattsburgh with questions concerning employment and benefits offered. Current Openings Assistant Director, Data Specialist — TRIO Student Support Services (SSS) The TRIO Student Support Services (SSS) program at SUNY Plattsburgh is seeking an\n                                          innovative, student-centered professional to serve as Assistant Director (Data Specialist).\n                                          This is an on-site position located at SUNY Plattsburgh. As an employee of The Research\n                                          Foundation for SUNY, this leadership position plays a vital role in advancing student\n                                          success through a combination of direct student support, data-informed decision making,\n                                          program assessment, and federal grant compliance. TRIO Student Support Services is a federally funded program dedicated to increasing\n                                          the retention, academic success, and graduation of first-generation college students,\n                                          students from modest-income backgrounds, and students with disabilities. Working collaboratively\n                                          with the Director and professional staff, the Assistant Director helps ensure high-quality\n                                          services while using data and assessment to continuously improve student outcomes\n                                          and program effectiveness. We believe data should tell the story of student success — not simply measure it.\n                                          The Assistant Director will use assessment, research, and student feedback to continually\n                                          improve services that help students thrive. Primary Responsibilities Provide academic advising, case management, needs assessments, and ongoing support\n                                             for an assigned caseload of students. Assist with student recruitment, applications, eligibility determination, intake appointments,\n                                             and records management. Co-instruct the TRIO Student Success Seminar (INT390) and support programming related\n                                             to academic success, financial literacy, career readiness, and student development. Lead data collection, assessment, program evaluation, budget reporting, and preparation\n                                             of required federal reports, including the Annual Performance Report (APR). Develop and implement continuous quality improvement processes that integrate student\n                                             outcomes, assessment results, participant feedback, and program evaluation to strengthen\n                                             services and support evidence-based decision making. Coordinate semester assessment activities, including Student Satisfaction Surveys\n                                             and Progress-to-Degree reviews, utilizing assessment findings and current research\n                                             to improve advising, programming, and service delivery. Supervise designated professional, graduate, and student staff by providing onboarding,\n                                             training, quality assurance, and ongoing professional guidance. Assist with planning and implementation of orientations, workshops, student engagement\n                                             activities, and other educational programming aligned with grant objectives. Collaborate with campus partners to strengthen student support services, improve operational\n                                             effectiveness, and enhance student success. Serve as the secondary administrator for the program and assume leadership responsibilities\n                                             in the Director’s absence. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Education, Social Work, Psychology, Counseling, Student Affairs,\n                                             Data Analytics, STEM, or a closely related field. Experience in student advising, case management, student support services, data collection,\n                                             analysis, reporting, and program assessment to support student success initiatives. Excellent organizational, analytical, interpersonal, and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities while working collaboratively within\n                                             a student-centered environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with first-generation college students, students from modest-income\n                                             backgrounds, and students with disabilities. Familiarity with higher education data systems and program assessment. Experience supporting FAFSA completion, financial literacy initiatives, and evidence-based\n                                             student success practices. Experience with federally funded grant programs, including compliance and reporting. Why Join TRIO Student Support Services? This is an opportunity to make a lasting impact on students’ lives while helping shape\n                                          the future of a nationally recognized student success program. The Assistant Director\n                                          will join a collaborative team committed to innovation, continuous improvement, and\n                                          providing comprehensive support that empowers students to persist, graduate, and achieve\n                                          their personal, academic, and professional goals. Salary Range Annual $58,000 – $75,000 commensurate with education, qualifications, and field experience.\n                                          Excellent benefit package. The Research Foundation is a private, nonprofit corporation, offering comprehensive\n                                          and low-cost health, dental, and vision insurance, basic and optional retirement plans,\n                                          employer paid life insurance, tuition waivers, paid time off, and other benefits. For full consideration, please apply by July 28, 2026. Submit vitae/resume, cover letter, list of 3 professional references to: Research Foundation for SUNY Box RF 2026-2 202 Kehoe Administration Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh, New York 12901 Fax: 518-564-2157 Email: [email protected] Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Education Specialist — Lake Champlain Research Institute The Research Foundation for the State University of New York at Plattsburgh (RF-SUNY)\n                                          is seeking a qualified candidate with technical and practical skills for the position\n                                          of Educator, to provide education and staff support with The Lake Champlain Research\n                                          Institute (LCRI) at SUNY Plattsburgh. SUNY Plattsburgh is a regional leader in environmental\n                                          science and ecology with strong undergraduate and graduate programs. The Lake Champlain\n                                          Research Institute is a hub for research on campus with many ongoing projects. The\n                                          Research Foundation is a private, nonprofit corporation, offering comprehensive and\n                                          low-cost health, dental, and vision insurance, basic and optional retirement plans,\n                                          employer paid life insurance, tuition waivers, paid time off, and other benefits. Job Description Function and Scope The Education Specialist will support ongoing outreach for the Lake Champlain Research\n                                          Institute to include the Lake Champlain Discovery Center. Responsibilities include\n                                          coordination of education activities, staffing the Center during operational hours,\n                                          implement education programs and support LCRI staff in the development of current\n                                          and future programs. Duties and Responsibilities Support ongoing outreach projects in LCRI focused on the Lake Champlain Discovery\n                                             Center. Coordinate education activities, including education space set up and design, implement\n                                             ongoing outreach center plans. Work with partners to develop materials, websites, outreach communications. Implement programs, support operational hours for programs. Support ongoing programs, maintenance of exhibits, order supplies, manage student\n                                             support teams. Required Qualifications B.S. or B.A. in Biology, Ecology, Environmental Science, or related fields and experience\n                                             with Lake Champlain outreach and education programs. Must have experience with environmental education and outreach planning and implementation. Evidence of organizational skills and working with student educators. Ability to work under general supervision, and collaboratively as part of a team. Certifications/Licenses Valid driver’s license Additional Information Salary Range: $40,000 to $45,000 commensurate with education, qualifications, and field experience.\n                                          Excellent benefit package. The Research Foundation is a private, nonprofit corporation, offering comprehensive\n                                          and low-cost health, dental, and vision insurance, basic and optional retirement plans,\n                                          employer paid life insurance, tuition waivers, paid time off, and other benefits. For full consideration, please apply by August 9, 2026. Submit vitae/resume, cover letter, list of 3 professional references to: Research Foundation for SUNY Box RF 2026-3 202 Kehoe Administration Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh, New York 12901 Fax: 518-564-2157 Email: [email protected] Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Coordinator of Instruction & Student Success Initiatives — TRIO Student Support Services The TRIO Student Support Services (SSS) program at SUNY Plattsburgh is seeking an\n                                          innovative, student-centered professional to serve as the Coordinator of Instruction\n                                          and Student Success Initiatives. This position reports to the Director of TRIO Student\n                                          Support Services (SSS) and serves as a member of the program’s leadership team. TRIO\n                                          SSS supports eligible undergraduate students who are first-generation, meet federal\n                                          income guidelines, and/or have a documented disability. Working within the broader Access and Opportunity Programs structure, the Coordinator\n                                          helps ensure that TRIO SSS students have access to coordinated academic support, compliant\n                                          course offerings, and meaningful opportunities to strengthen their academic, career,\n                                          and transferable skills. The position works collaboratively with students, TRIO SSS\n                                          staff, AOP leadership, faculty, campus partners, employers, alumni, and community\n                                          organizations. Primary Responsibilities Instruction and course coordination: Coordinate TRIO SSS-supported courses and instructional initiatives, including communication\n                                             with faculty and academic departments, enrollment monitoring, student support, assessment,\n                                             and compliance with grant and institutional requirements. Tutoring and academic support: Coordinate TRIO SSS student access to tutoring, supplemental instruction, and other\n                                             academic support services within the broader AOP structure; identify areas of student\n                                             need and help evaluate participation and outcomes. Student success programming: Develop and facilitate courses, workshops, and other learning opportunities that\n                                             strengthen academic success, leadership, communication, problem-solving, self-advocacy,\n                                             professionalism, and other transferable skills. Internships and experiential learning:\n                                             Help students identify and prepare for internships, employment, undergraduate research,\n                                             mentoring, service learning, and other high-impact educational experiences aligned\n                                             with their academic and career goals. Scholarship and opportunity support: Coordinate outreach and student support related to TRIO, institutional, and external\n                                             scholarships and funding opportunities that increase access to academic and career-building\n                                             experiences. Individualized student support: Maintain an assigned student caseload, assist students in establishing academic and\n                                             career goals, provide proactive outreach, and connect students with appropriate campus\n                                             and community resources. Program leadership and assessment: Contribute to TRIO SSS planning, assessment, reporting, and continuous improvement;\n                                             maintain accurate records of services and outcomes and supervise designated graduate\n                                             or student staff as assigned. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in education, counseling, student affairs, higher education, social\n                                             work, curriculum and instruction, career development, or a closely related field. Experience working with college students through teaching, advising, coaching, mentoring,\n                                             academic support, or a related student-success role. Experience developing or facilitating\n                                             courses, workshops, training, or other structured learning experiences. Demonstrated ability to coordinate programs, manage multiple priorities, and collaborate\n                                             with a variety of campus and community partners. Strong organizational, written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills. Experience using student participation, feedback, or outcome data to inform and improve\n                                             services. Demonstrated commitment to supporting first-generation students, students with financial\n                                             need, students with disabilities, and students from historically underserved backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications Experience with TRIO, opportunity programs, access programs, or similar student-success\n                                             initiatives. College-level teaching or curriculum-development experience. Experience coordinating tutoring, supplemental instruction, internships, career-readiness\n                                             programming, scholarships, or other high-impact practices. Experience supervising, training, or mentoring graduate or student staff. Familiarity with grant-funded programming, program assessment, or compliance-related\n                                             documentation. Experience using student information, case-management, learning-management, or program\n                                             database systems. Why Join TRIO Student Support Services? This is an opportunity to make a lasting impact on students’ lives while helping shape\n                                          the future of a nationally recognized student success program. The Coordinator of\n                                          Instruction and Student Success Initiatives will join a collaborative team committed\n                                          to innovation, continuous improvement, and providing comprehensive support that empowers\n                                          students to persist, graduate, and achieve their personal, academic, and professional\n                                          goals. Experience: Three to five years of progressive experience in higher education, student support,\n                                          instruction, advising, program coordination, supervision, career-readiness, or experiential-learning\n                                          initiatives. Salary Range: $58,000 – $70,000 and excellent fringe benefit package. The Research Foundation is a private, nonprofit corporation, offering comprehensive\n                                          and low-cost health, dental, and vision insurance, basic and optional retirement plans,\n                                          employer paid life insurance, tuition waivers, paid time off, and other benefits. For full consideration, please apply by August 21, 2026. Applicants review will begin\n                                          immediately. Research Foundation for SUNY Box RF 2026-3 202 Kehoe Administration Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh, New York 12901 Fax: 518-564-2157 Email: [email protected] If an applicant cannot complete the application process to respond to a notice of\n                           job vacancy due to a disability or other concern, please contact the Research Foundation\n                           Human Resources Office at SUNY Plattsburgh: 518-564-2132 . Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer As an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer, The Research Foundation for SUNY\n                              will not discriminate in its employment practices due to an applicant's race, color,\n                              creed, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions),\n                              sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, transgender status, age, national\n                              origin, marital status, citizenship, physical and mental disability, criminal record,\n                              genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, status with respect to receiving\n                              public assistance, domestic violence victim status, a disabled, special, recently\n                              separated, active duty wartime, campaign badge, Armed Forces service medal veteran,\n                              or any other characteristics protected under applicable law. The company will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against applicants\n                              because they have inquired about, or discussed their own pay or the pay of another\n                              employee of applicant. The Research Foundation for the State University of New York is not an agency or instrumentality\n                           of the State of New York. Employees of the Research Foundation for the State University\n                           of New York are not state employees, do not participate in any state retirement system,\n                           and do not receive state fringe benefits. The Research Foundation for the State University\n                           of New York operates under a contract with The State University of New York and receives\n                           no directly appropriated state funding. Sponsored Research & Programs Auditory Research Laboratory Faculty Development Workshops Funding Opportunities Preparing Proposals Prospective Employees Upward Bound Staff Contact Us Yvonne Lott Associate Director/Human Resource Coordinator 206 Kehoe Administration Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-2132 [email protected] Sponsored Research Office Sponsored Research & Programs Auditory Research Laboratory Faculty Development Workshops Funding Opportunities Preparing Proposals Prospective Employees Upward Bound Staff Contact Us Yvonne Lott Associate Director/Human Resource Coordinator 206 Kehoe Administration Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-2132 [email protected] Sponsored Research Office Jump to Header Plattsburgh State University of New York Like us on Facebook. Find us on Instagram. Connect with us on Snapchat. Connect with us on LinkedIn. Login required. Watch us on YouTube. Virtual Tour Employment Emergency Info Find People Consumer Info Accessibility Title IX Feinberg Library Bookstore 101 Broad Street , Plattsburgh, NY 12901 • 518-564-2000 Copyright © 1996 – Privacy Policy Contact Us Last Updated 8/31/26 Back to top"
    },
    "https://www.cs.ny.gov/jobseeker/public/cr.cfm": {
      "title": "Department of Civil Service",
      "description": "Continuous Recruitment Examinations Navigation menu Department of Civil Service Online Services Account Login Apply Online My Examination Applications Eligible Lists (ELMS Online) Job Seekers Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement (HELP) program Centers for Careers in Government (CCG) State Examinations Local Examinations Veterans & Individuals With Disabilities Student Internships StateJobsNY New York State Fellowship Programs State Employees State Examinations Health Benefits Resources Paid Family Leave Paid Parental Leave Career Mobility Office Retirees Health Benefits Resources Retirement Benefits Working After Retirement HR Professionals State Government Local Government Civil Service Institute About Us About Us Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Sections Overview Minimum Education and Experience Advanced Degree Required or Professional Certification and/or Licensing Required Open to Current State Employees New York State Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement Statewide (NY HELPS) Continuous Recruitment Examinations Overview Applications for most continuous recruitment examinations are accepted continuously, with no application deadline. Examinations are conducted whenever there is a need for qualified individuals. Minimum Education and Work Experience Required These are jobs that are filled through continuous recruitment examinations. In order to qualify for the examination, you must meet the minimum qualifications of educational and work experience, which is listed on the examination announcement. Correction Officer Trainee Correction Officers are responsible for the custody and security as well as the safety and well-being of incarcerated individuals in State Correctional Facilities, Shock Incarceration Correctional Facilities, Work Release Centers and Drug Treatment Campuses. Information Technology Specialist Information Technology Specialists perform or assist in performing technical and agency program support IT activities related to network and system design, configuration, maintenance, and security; customer support; business/systems analysis and design which may include web site development and administration of a transactional, dynamic, or interactive web site; and the design, development and administration of database systems. Please be advised, the current open competitive examinations for Information Technology Specialists have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Current list eligibles can access the Skills Inventory to update as frequently as every six months here: Online Questionnaire Selection for State Government (ny.gov) NOTE: The promotion examination for Information Technology Specialist 2 is still open for application and can be found here: Information Technology Specialist 2 Promotion Examination(ny.gov) Optometric Technician Optometric Technicians provide eye and vision care services to patients. Based on State licensing regulations and assignment, the positions measure facial features to ensure proper sizing of lenses and frames, advise patients on frame and spectacle lens selection, order frames and lenses, check lens prescriptions for accuracy upon return from the laboratory, dispense patient prescriptions after making all necessary adjustments and modifications, and advise patients on contact lens selection, application, and cleaning of contact lenses based on the eye care provider's prescription. Please be advised, this examination has been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible list will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible list or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage should be directed to the State University of New York, College of Optometry, Office of Human Resources at 212-938-5882 Plant Utilities Assistant Plant Utilities Assistants assist in the operation, maintenance and repair of mechanical and electrical equipment providing heat, hot water, ventilation, air-conditioning and electrical distribution. Please be advised, these examinations have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage should be directed to the agency you applied to. The following page provides a list of participating agencies and their direct contact information: Plant Utilities Agency Contact Information Transportation Construction Inspector » Transportation Construction Inspectors perform testing on various materials used in the construction of roads and bridges, support professional engineering staff in construction compliance activities, and perform construction and/or material inspections for assigned projects. Verbatim Reporter Verbatim Reports take and transcribe verbatim records at hearings, formal meetings and conferences in judicial and quasi-judicial matters, and in other venues where verbatim transcription of spoken material or audio recordings is required. Please be advised, this examination has been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible list will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible list or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage should be directed to the Workers Compensation Board at: HumanResourcesManagementBureau@wcb.ny.gov Advanced Degree Required or Professional Certification and/or Licensing Required These jobs are also filled through continuous recruitment examinations. In order to qualify for the examination, \r\n\t\tyou must have an advanced degree in the area(s) of study listed on the examination announcement. For some jobs, in order to qualify, you may also be required to possess professional certification or licensure as listed on the examination announcement. Actuary Positions Actuaries perform actuarial computations relative to insurance plans and rates of contribution to pension funds, and for the preparation of the mortality, disability and other demographic tables upon which such calculations are based. Incumbents determine reserves to provide future benefits and analyze sources of earnings under policies and contracts to determine proper rates of dividends and other indeterminate credits and charges. Please be advised, these examinations have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage should be directed to the agency you applied to. The following page provides a list of participating agencies and their direct contact information: Actuary Positions - Agency Contact Information Auditor 1 (Abandoned Property) | Auditor Trainee 1 (Abandoned Property) Auditor 1 (Abandoned Property) review banks, insurance companies, utilities, stockbrokers, collateral loan makers or any other organization that may hold unclaimed property to ensure accurate and complete reporting and remittance of unclaimed property to the State Comptroller. Please be advised, these examinations have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage, should be directed to Office of the State Comptroller (OSC) at Email: recruit@osc.ny.gov or Phone: (518) 474-1924 Auditor 1 (Municipal) | Auditor Trainee 1 (Municipal) Auditor 1 (Municipal) review annual financial information submitted by local government entities, conduct financial and performance audits; provide technical assistance, and other functions analyzing and evaluating local government fiscal health. Please be advised, these examinations have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage, should be directed to Office of the State Comptroller (OSC) at Email: recruit@osc.ny.gov or Phone: (518) 474-1924 Auditor Trainee 1 (Tax) | Auditor 1 (Tax) Auditor 1 (Tax) perform on-site field audits and examinations of taxpayers' books, records, and substantiating data to determine compliance with various articles of the New York State Tax Law. Please be advised, these examinations have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. The eligible lists will remain active. Applications will no longer be accepted. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage, should be directed to the Department of Taxation and Finance. Engineering Positions Engineering careers are available to college graduates in engineering and engineering technology, individuals \r\n\t\twho have passed the National Council of Examiners for Engineering and Surveying (NCEES) Fundamentals of Engineering (FE) \r\n\t\texamination, and New York State licensed and currently registered Professional Engineers. Please be advised, the open competitive examinations for Engineers have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. The eligible lists will remain active. Applications will no longer be accepted. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage should be directed to the agency you applied to. The following page provides a list of participating agencies and their direct contact information: Agency Contact Information NOTE:The promotion examinations for Professional Engineers are still open for application and can be found here: New York State Career Opportunities in Engineering (ny.gov) Information Technology Specialist Information Technology Specialists perform or assist in performing technical and agency program support IT activities related to network and system design, configuration, maintenance, and security; customer support; business/systems analysis and design which may include web site development and administration of a transactional, dynamic, or interactive web site; and the design, development and administration of database systems. Please be advised, the current open competitive examinations for Information Technology Specialists have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Current list eligibles can access the Skills Inventory to update as frequently as every six months here: Online Questionnaire Selection for State Government (ny.gov) The promotion examination for Information Technology Specialist 2 is still open for application and can be found here: Information Technology Specialist 2 Promotion Examination - Job Seekers - Department of Civil Service (ny.gov) Legal Specialties Attorneys may perform a wide range of assignments and the tasks performed vary considerably. There are some who as members of a very small legal office receive wide ranging assignments, while others, usually in larger offices, receive a more limited variety of work. Please be advised, this examination has been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible list will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible list or NY HELPS to make appointments. Current list eligibles can access the Skills Inventory for updates here: Online Questionnaire Selection for State Government (ny.gov) Licensed Psychologist Licensed Psychologists provide professional psychological services and/or supervise psychological services provided by clinical and non-licensed psychology staff. License and currently registered to practice psychology in New York State required. Please be advised, these examinations have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. NOTE: The promotion examinations for Licensed Psychologists are still open for application and can be found here: Scheduled Continuous Recruitment Promotion Examinations (ny.gov) Nursing Positions » Nurses (registered professional nurses) conduct health assessments; diagnose and treat an individuals' responses to actual, potential, or diagnosed health problems through the provision of care supportive to or restorative of life and well-being; and execute medical regimens prescribed by a licensed health care provider. Nurses also serve on interdisciplinary health care teams and health related committees to plan and implement health care. Optician Opticians provide eye and vision care services to patients. Based on State licensing regulations and assignment, the positions measure facial features to ensure proper sizing of lenses and frames, advise patients on frame and spectacle lens selection, order frames and lenses, check lens prescriptions for accuracy upon return from the laboratory, dispense patient prescriptions after making all necessary adjustments and modifications, and advise patients on contact lens selection, application, and cleaning of contact lenses based on the eye care providers prescription. Please be advised, this examination has been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible list will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible list or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage should be directed to the State University of New York, College of Optometry, Office of Human Resources at 212-938-5882 Plant Utilities Engineer Plant Utilities Engineers operates, maintains, troubleshoots, repairs, tests, and calibrates mechanical and electrical equipment providing heat, hot water, ventilation, air-conditioning and electrical distribution in the most efficient and safe manner possible. Incumbents also make recommendations on major overhauls and replacement of equipment and initiate activity relating to energy conservation projects. Please be advised, these examinations have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage should be directed to the agency you applied to. The following page provides a list of participating agencies and their direct contact information: Plant Utilities Positions - Agency Contact Information Psychiatric Examiner (Psychologist) License and currently registered to practice psychology in New York State required Department Of Civil Service Please be advised, this examination has been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible list will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible list or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage, should be directed to the New York State Office of Mental Health (OMH) at 518-474-2413, or by Email at: OMHHRM@omh.ny.gov State Program Examiner | State Program Examiner Trainee 1 State Program Examiners assist in the financial and performance audits of all state departments, agencies, \r\n\t\tinstitutions and authorities, directed at financial accountability, management effectiveness and efficiency, and program \r\n\t\tperformance. Please be advised, these examinations have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible lists or NY HELPS to make appointments. Questions about eligible list usage, should be directed to Office of the State Comptroller (OSC) at Email: recruit@osc.ny.gov or Phone: (518) 474-1924. Teaching Positions Teachers deal with learners having a broad range of physical and mental aptitudes, abilities, interests, social and academic backgrounds and ages in addition to some behavioral physical, mental or emotional problems. - Applications will be accepted during October of each year. Please be advised, these examinations have been suspended effective March 1, 2024. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible lists will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible list or NY HELPS to make appointments. Vulnerable Persons Protection Specialist 1 Please be advised this examination has been suspended. Applications will no longer be accepted. The eligible list will remain active. Agencies will have the option to utilize the active eligible list or NY HELPS to make appointments. Open to Current State Employees There are also continuous recruitment examinations open to all qualified current State employees. These examinations are called promotion or transition examinations . Some examinations are conducted by the Department of Civil Service, while others are conducted by the agencies where the positions exist. There is no application deadline for these examinations, which are held based on the need for qualified individuals. New York State Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement Statewide (NY HELPS) To address staffing issues in State agencies, the Department of Civil Service implemented the NY HELPS program to streamline the appointment process. At this time, the titles included in the program do not require examination. Some of the titles approved NY HELPS were previously Continuous Recruitment examinations. At this time, previously Continuous Recruitment titles included in the NY HELPS program do not require examination. If you are seeking information about specific titles, the Glossary of Titles (GOT-IT) search tool will provide answers to your questions. GOT-IT will also indicate if the title is included in the NY HELPS program. To find more information about the NY HELPS program, visit our NY HELPS webpage . For all other open titles and positions, please visit the Statejobs website. Top Department Of Civil Service About Us Agency Overview Executive Leadership Law, Rules & Regulations Stay Informed Join #TeamCivilService Press Releases Get Help Contact Civil Service Equal Opportunity Policy Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Language Access Information Reasonable Accommodation Resources Public Information Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) Eligible Lists (ELMS Online) Open Meetings Test Guides & Resource Booklets Vendor Information DPM-100 Master Equal Employment Opportunity Data Collection Form Executive Order 31 Online Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Policy CONNECT WITH US FACEBOOK INSTAGRAM LINKEDIN YOUTUBE TWITTER REGISTER TO VOTE Sign up online or download and mail in your application REGISTER NOW"
    },
