    "https://www.cs.ny.gov/jobseeker/public/stateexam.cfm": {
      "title": "Department of Civil Service",
      "description": "Working for New York State Navigation menu Department of Civil Service Online Services Account Login Apply Online My Examination Applications Eligible Lists (ELMS Online) Job Seekers Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement (HELP) program Centers for Careers in Government (CCG) State Examinations Local Examinations Veterans & Individuals With Disabilities Student Internships StateJobsNY New York State Fellowship Programs State Employees State Examinations Health Benefits Resources Paid Family Leave Paid Parental Leave Career Mobility Office Retirees Health Benefits Resources Retirement Benefits Working After Retirement HR Professionals State Government Local Government Civil Service Institute About Us About Us Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Working for New York State Rewarding Careers in Public Service Start Here. Access important resources including civil service examination announcements, featured programs, and information \r\n\t\t\tregarding current job vacancies. Sections Working in State Government Finding Career Opportunities State Examination Announcements Applying for an Examination After Taking the Examination Online Examinations Additional Information Working in State Government State government is comprised of a diverse and dedicated workforce who provides valuable services to millions of their fellow New Yorkers. New York State hires individuals who are afforded almost limitless opportunities that touch every part of public life — including education, environmental conservation, and even health care. The State employs people of all ages, backgrounds, and education levels — from first responders to engineers, nurses, research scientists, plow drivers, and more. In addition to the exciting and diverse job opportunities, State employees also receive comprehensive compensation packages, including excellent health and retirement benefits and work-life balance options, such as flexible work hours and alternative work schedules. To learn about employment opportunities across State government,  including the hiring process, information about civil service examinations, and other featured job programs, please watch our three-part video series: Finding Career Opportunities Appointments and promotions in State government are made according to the principles of \"merit and fitness,\" as mandated by the \r\n\t\tState Constitution. The State offers many career  opportunities, including both non-competitive roles and those that require  participation in civil service examinations. Find Non-Competitive Careers: positions that do NOT require an exam NY Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement Statewide (NY HELPS) is a program that temporarily removes the civil service exam requirement for thousands of positions across State agencies. To view open jobs, please visit State Jobs. To narrow your search for NY HELPS jobs, click on \"For the General Public\". Select \"YES\" in the NY HELPS field. Press submit. This will bring up all of the NY HELPS jobs that are available. Internship Opportunities provides       a centralized location to access all State Government internships. Veterans Temporary Hiring Program provides a centralized location for       qualifying veterans to submit up-to-date employment and contact       information for consideration by state agencies when filling temporary       positions. Governor's Program to Hire       Individuals and Veterans with Disabilities provides a centralized location for       55-b/c job seekers to submit up-to-date employment and contact information       for consideration by state agencies filling entry-level positions. Compete in Civil Service Examinations Civil service examinations assess candidates' knowledge, skills, and abilities necessary for performing the job. The type of test to be used on a particular examination will depend upon the nature of the job involved and will be specified on the examination announcement under \"Subject of Examination.\" State Examination Announcements Please Note: For the period of May 2024 to June 2026, testing requirements will be waived for most open-competitive positions through the NY HELPS Program. Examination announcements provide important information about each examination being held, including the job title(s), date of the examination,  location, duties, salary, the subject of the examination, deadline to apply, and fee information. When you are interested in taking an examination, first review the announcement to  determine if you are eligible. There are minimum qualifications for all examinations which you must meet in order to participate in the examination. Experience in a particular field of work may be required for some jobs. Other jobs also will require a demonstration of proficiency at certain skills, such as typing or fluency in a second language, or require a physical examination. Read each examination announcement carefully. You must meet the qualifications in order to take the examination. Most examinations are held periodically. Some examinations are held continuously, with applications accepted anytime. With these continuous recruitment examinations, the qualified applicants are tested on an as-needed basis, and successful candidates' names are added to the eligible list continuously. Archived examination announcements , which contain information such as minimum qualifications at the time the examinations were given, are posted\r\n\t\tfor reference purposes only and cannot be used when applying for upcoming examinations. Examinations Open to the Public Examinations Open to State Employees Continuous Recruitment Examinations Applying for an Examination You can apply on-line or download the announcement and appropriate application. Your application will be reviewed to ensure that you meet the minimum qualifications listed on the examination announcement. You can apply for most State examinations online . To apply for an examination online you will need to sign in using your ny.gov ID. If you do not have an ny.gov ID, please create an account . Some features of the online application process include being able to save and return to an application you did not complete . You can also see a list of examinations you have already applied for using the online application process. After you apply, you will receive a notification indicating whether you are approved to take the examination. After Taking an Examination After taking an examination, you will be notified by email when official scores are available online, usually within 90 - 120 days of the examination date. Eligible lists and score notices are available on the Eligible List Management System (ELMS) . After you receive your score for an examination, you should check ELMS regularly for job canvasses from State Agencies. You may also receive canvass notifications at the email address you have designated, but you should continue checking ELMS to ensure that no job canvass opportunities are missed. If you have taken a promotion examination, you will be assigned a promotion unit code that aligns with the agency you were at when you applied for the examination. These promotion unit codes are important specifically when a list is tied to several agencies as it informs your place on the list. If after you applied for the examination, you moved to a new agency, you may be eligible to have your promotion unit code updated to your new agency. For more information about promotional exam unit codes, please read our Advisory Memo #89-02 . To ask to update your promotion unit code or if you have any other question regarding your status, you may also email our List Maintenance Unit at EmploymentRecords@cs.ny.gov . For Frequently Asked Questions regarding what happens after taking an examination, visit the FAQ page. Online Examinations (login required) Training and Experience Examinations Online questionnaires for State Government positions. You can complete some training and experience examinations online such as Information Technology Specialist, State Program Examiner, Professional Engineer, and others. Additional Information How to find a job with New York State published by the Department of Civil Service. Current openings for the public and opportunities for current state employees. Professional Career Opportunities is one exam that is used by state agencies to fill more than 100 different entry-level professional job types across a wide range of disciplines. Test guides published by the Department of Civil Service for state and local government examinations. Eligible List Management System (ELMS Online) allows you to view eligible lists, score notices, canvass letters, and related information. Evaluations of Foreign Education a current list of accepted companies which can provide foreign degree equivalency evaluations. Sign up here to be notified by email of upcoming examination announcements. Get Updates Top Department Of Civil Service About Us Agency Overview Executive Leadership Law, Rules & Regulations Stay Informed Join #TeamCivilService Press Releases Get Help Contact Civil Service Equal Opportunity Policy Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Language Access Information Reasonable Accommodation Resources Public Information Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) Eligible Lists (ELMS Online) Open Meetings Test Guides & Resource Booklets Vendor Information DPM-100 Master Equal Employment Opportunity Data Collection Form Executive Order 31 Online Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Policy CONNECT WITH US FACEBOOK INSTAGRAM LINKEDIN YOUTUBE TWITTER REGISTER TO VOTE Sign up online or download and mail in your application REGISTER NOW"
    },
    "https://www.plattsburgh.edu/about/offices-divisions/administration-finance/human-resources/jobs/index.html": {
      "title": "Professional, Academic & Civil Service Jobs",
      "description": "Professional, Academic & Civil Service Jobs at SUNY Plattsburgh | SUNY Plattsburgh twitter brain business compass computer environment exit-site globe graph handshake health justice measure networking open-pdf pencil science trend video world arrow-right bars blogger caret-down caret-left caret-right caret-up close facebook gears home instagram linkedin logo play plus quote search snapchat-ghost tumblr virtual-tour women-network world-globe youtube-play logo-white Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Jump to Main Content Plattsburgh State University of New York Site Search Search Search SUNY Plattsburgh Visit Us Visit Apply Now Apply Request Info Info Academics Majors & Minors Online Programs Graduate Programs Microcredentials Schools & Departments Queensbury Campus Career Development Center Honors Program Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Academic Advising Feinberg Library Learning Center Study Abroad & Exchanges Technology Services Admissions First-Year Transfer Graduate International Readmission Educational Opportunity Program Non-Matriculated Students Registration Dates & Forms Apply Now Check Your Application Status Request More Information Visit & Event Options Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Scholarships, Loans & Grants Work Study & Student Jobs Apply for Aid Bill Paying & Refunds Net Price Calculator Graduate Student Aid Current Student Financial Aid Financial Services Forms PlattsLife Calendar of Events Activities & Getting Involved Campus Housing & Community Living Food & Dining Virtual Tour Our Location Visual & Performing Arts Campus TV & Radio Stations Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Health & Safety Career Development Center Student Support & Resources First Year Student Programs Commencement Sustainability Athletics Cardinal Athletics Recreational Sports & Programs Facilities Fitness Center Ticket Sales About Us President & Leadership Campus News Offices & Divisions Centers, Institutes & Clinics SUNY Plattsburgh at Queensbury Plattsburgh Next Mission, Vision & Values University Profile Consumer Information College Auxiliary Services Campus Facilities Directions & Campus Maps MyPlattsburgh Make a Gift Who are you? Current Students Parents & Families School Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Community Jump to Footer Go back to the SUNY Plattsburgh Home Page About SUNY Plattsburgh Offices & Divisions Division of Administration & Finance Human Resource & Payroll Services Professional, Academic & Civil Service Jobs Professional, Academic & Civil Service Jobs at SUNY Plattsburgh SUNY Plattsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to excellence through\n                              diversity. We are a residential campus, located in a small city in upstate New York near the\n                              Canada and Vermont borders. It is walkable, safe and scenic — a great university and\n                              community environment with a never ending list of activities to try and places to\n                              visit. View Current SUNY Plattsburgh Openings View Current Research Foundation Openings Living & Working Here SUNY Plattsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to excellence through\n                           diversity. We offer health, dental and vision insurances, as well as various retirement plans. And,\n                              eligible appointees may receive moving reimbursement if certain criteria are met. We support our students by providing a vibrant campus atmosphere full of intercollegiate\n                              athletics, intramural sports and student organizations. In order to fully engage our\n                              students, it is crucial that most employees report to campus to fulfill their work\n                              obligations.  We recognize there are some exceptions such as those employees that\n                              work at our branch campus — SUNY Plattsburgh at Queensbury — those working exclusively with online degree programs or a limited number of professional\n                              positions with a unique work location.  All teaching modalities should be discussed\n                              with the appropriate chair/dean. Learn more about the benefits of working for the State University of New York at Plattsburgh. Learn more about our school profile . Things to Do, Where to Stay, Where to Eat — we invite you to explore the Adirondack Coast. Search Housing Information — Information and listings brought to you by the North Country Chamber of Commerce EXPLORE OUR LOCATION Employment Resources New York State Civil Service Exam Announcements Continuous Recruitment Exams — Open to all qualified individuals Scheduled Exams — Open to all qualified individuals Continuous Recruitment Exams — Open to state employees Scheduled Promotion Exams — Open to state employees Internal Promotions Management and the UUP bargaining unit at SUNY Plattsburgh share the responsibility\n                                          of supporting and retaining a strong, creative and proactive workforce. The workforce\n                                          of our university is the core element of future success and prosperity, and the parameters\n                                          outlined in this document have been devised with the goal of acknowledging the value\n                                          of the employees who devote their professional lives to SUNY Plattsburgh. View Internal Promotion Plan Other Employment Options on Campus Student Jobs Campus Dining — Food Service Jobs Sponsored Research Jobs Applying to & Working at SUNY Plattsburgh FAQs Who is responsible for employment reference checking and education verification? The hiring department is responsible for verifying degree completion and employment\n                                          references. All information must be verified prior to the offer of employment. Employment References\n                                          for most positions will be done electronically by Human Resource and Payroll Services\n                                          through VidCruiter. This electronic reference check is coordinated by email and is a crucial step in the\n                                          hiring process, so timely completion is necessary. All employees hired for a position with a degree requirement will need to provide\n                                          original transcripts prior to the start of employment. What employment opportunities do you have available for clerical (Civil Service),\n                                    maintenance, professional, or teaching positions? Vacancies can be found on the Human Resource and Payroll Services Jobs website . All applications are processed electronically through this website. Chromebooks are\n                                          available for use in the Human Resource and Payroll Services office (912 Kehoe) for\n                                          those individuals who do not have access to the web. Can I apply for a Civil Service vacancy? Please review the qualifications of each individual posting carefully.  You can apply\n                                          if you meet the minimum qualifications listed.  Some vacancies require that you have\n                                          taken a civil service exam and you would have to return a canvass letter for that\n                                          specific vacancy for consideration. Otherwise, you can apply if you are a permanent employee at the college and meet the\n                                          posted qualifications for the position. Employees from other state agencies who are\n                                          interested and eligible to transfer to a posted vacancy should check our Jobs website\n                                          often and apply directly to whichever position interests you. You may be contacted by Human Resource and Payroll Services for additional information\n                                          in order to verify your eligibility to transfer. Will I get an interview for a Civil Service vacancy if I received a canvass letter? A canvass letter is merely an announcement that a vacancy exists in the title for\n                                       which an individual was tested. A person must be reachable (one of the top three scores\n                                       of those individuals who responded interested) to be eligible for an interview. How do I know which Civil Service Exams are being given and when? Visit the Civil Service website for information on up-coming exams. What is an I-9 form and why do I have to show originals as supporting documentation? The I-9 is a federally required document that verifies that an individual is eligible\n                                       for employment in this country. According to the rules governing the completion of\n                                       the I-9, only original documents can be used. You can find the required documentation\n                                       listed on page two of the I-9 form: one document from list “A” OR one each from lists\n                                       “B” and “C”. How often do I have to complete an I-9 form? US citizens: I-9’s are valid continuously unless a break of employment occurs. If\n                                          an employee is rehired within 3 years of the date that a previous Form I-9 was completed,\n                                          the employer may either request a new Form I-9, or complete Section 3 of the previously\n                                          completed Form I-9. If the employer previously completed Section 3, or if the version\n                                          of the form used for a previous verification is no longer valid, Section 3 of a new\n                                          Form I-9 must be completed using the most current version and attached to the previously\n                                          completed Form I-9. Also, if any supporting documentation is expired, you may have\n                                          to provide updated documents. If a rehire occurs after 3 years from the initial date\n                                          of execution of the Form I-9, a new Form I-9 must be completed. International employees on H-1B (specialty occupation) or J-1 (exchange visitor) visas\n                                          must have their I-9 updated each time their visa is renewed. In the event of a name change, new supporting documentation is also required. How can I get an official campus ID card? During your orientation with Human Resource and Payroll Services, you will receive\n                                       a temporary ID card. Take this card to the ID card office in Clinton Dining Hall to\n                                       have your picture taken and they will give you an official campus ID card. Can a part-time professional staff appointee (academic or professional employee) be\n                                    granted tenure? The Policies of the Board of Trustees of the State University of New York exclude\n                                       part-time service in determining eligibility for tenure. [Reference Article XI, Title\n                                       B (for academic employees) and Article XI, Title C (for professional employees) of\n                                       the Policies.] Can a person appointed to qualified academic rank be given a term appointment? Yes. Appointees to qualified academic rank may be appointed to temporary or term appointments.\n                                       They receive all other benefits and terms and conditions of employment except that\n                                       their time in qualified academic rank does not count towards meeting the “academic\n                                       rank” service requirements for tenure. How is compensation determined for a professional employee at hire or promotion? Many factors are involved. Learn more in the Professional Employees' Compensation and Promotion Plan . General Information about SUNY Plattsburgh Safety & Security SUNY Plattsburgh’s Annual Security Report includes statistics for the previous three\n                                          years concerning reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings\n                                          or property owned or controlled by SUNY Plattsburgh; and on public property within,\n                                          or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes\n                                          institutional policies/procedures concerning campus security, such as policies/procedures\n                                          concerning sexual assault and other matters. Copies of this report may be requested by contacting University Police at [email protected] or accessed digitally on the University Police website: UPD Statistics and Resources . Information can also be obtained from the U.S. Department of Education . Americans with Disabilities Act & Accommodation In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and applicable federal\n                                             and state laws, SUNY Plattsburgh is committed to providing equal employment opportunity\n                                             and reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities.\n                                             Reasonable accommodations are provided to ensure access to the application, interview,\n                                             and selection process for applicants and to enable employees to perform the essential\n                                             functions of their positions. Individuals are not required to disclose a disability\n                                             unless requesting an accommodation. Requests for reasonable accommodation must be\n                                             made in a timely manner and supported by appropriate documentation, as required. All\n                                             disability-related information will be maintained in a confidential manner. Applicants\n                                             and employees seeking reasonable accommodation should contact Human Resource and Payroll\n                                             Services at 518-564-5062. Compensation Disclosure Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order,\n                                          is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide\n                                          his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time\n                                          as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation.\n                                          If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the\n                                          Office of Employee Relations at 518-474-6988 or via email at [email protected] . Non-Discrimination Policy The Non-Discrimination Policy provides guidance and information on policies and procedures,\n                                          and a mechanism to explain how SUNY Plattsburgh defines, responds to, and resolves\n                                          incidents of discrimination and/or harassment. Notice of Non-Discrimination Policy Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Statement SUNY Plattsburgh is fully committed to excellence through diversity, equity and inclusion,\n                                          and to supporting a welcoming environment for all students, employees and visitors.\n                                          As an equal opportunity employer and a government contractor subject to the Vietnam\n                                          Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA), the university guarantees equitable\n                                          consideration to all qualified applicants with regard to race, color, national origin,\n                                          religion, creed, age, ability, assigned gender, gender identity, sexual orientation,\n                                          familial status, economic status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics,\n                                          military status, domestic violence victim status, criminal conviction, or any other\n                                          legally protected status per federal or state laws. Jobs — Recruitment Internal Professional Promotion Plan Recruitment & Online Recruiting System Contact Us Human Resource & Payroll Services 912 Kehoe Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-5062 Fax: 518-564-5060 [email protected] Jobs — Recruitment Internal Professional Promotion Plan Recruitment & Online Recruiting System Contact Us Human Resource & Payroll Services 912 Kehoe Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-5062 Fax: 518-564-5060 [email protected] Jump to Header Plattsburgh State University of New York Like us on Facebook. Find us on Instagram. Connect with us on Snapchat. Connect with us on LinkedIn. Login required. Watch us on YouTube. Virtual Tour Employment Emergency Info Find People Consumer Info Accessibility Title IX Feinberg Library Bookstore 101 Broad Street , Plattsburgh, NY 12901 • 518-564-2000 Copyright © 1996 – Privacy Policy Contact Us Last Updated 8/31/26 Back to top"
    },
    "https://www.plattsburgh.edu/about/offices-divisions/administration-finance/human-resources/jobs/internal-professional-plan.html": {
      "title": "Internal Professional Promotion Plan for Faculty & Staff",
      "description": "Internal Professional Promotion Plan | SUNY Plattsburgh twitter brain business compass computer environment exit-site globe graph handshake health justice measure networking open-pdf pencil science trend video world arrow-right bars blogger caret-down caret-left caret-right caret-up close facebook gears home instagram linkedin logo play plus quote search snapchat-ghost tumblr virtual-tour women-network world-globe youtube-play logo-white Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Jump to Main Content Plattsburgh State University of New York Site Search Search Search SUNY Plattsburgh Visit Us Visit Apply Now Apply Request Info Info Academics Majors & Minors Online Programs Graduate Programs Microcredentials Schools & Departments Queensbury Campus Career Development Center Honors Program Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Academic Advising Feinberg Library Learning Center Study Abroad & Exchanges Technology Services Admissions First-Year Transfer Graduate International Readmission Educational Opportunity Program Non-Matriculated Students Registration Dates & Forms Apply Now Check Your Application Status Request More Information Visit & Event Options Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Scholarships, Loans & Grants Work Study & Student Jobs Apply for Aid Bill Paying & Refunds Net Price Calculator Graduate Student Aid Current Student Financial Aid Financial Services Forms PlattsLife Calendar of Events Activities & Getting Involved Campus Housing & Community Living Food & Dining Virtual Tour Our Location Visual & Performing Arts Campus TV & Radio Stations Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Health & Safety Career Development Center Student Support & Resources First Year Student Programs Commencement Sustainability Athletics Cardinal Athletics Recreational Sports & Programs Facilities Fitness Center Ticket Sales About Us President & Leadership Campus News Offices & Divisions Centers, Institutes & Clinics SUNY Plattsburgh at Queensbury Plattsburgh Next Mission, Vision & Values University Profile Consumer Information College Auxiliary Services Campus Facilities Directions & Campus Maps MyPlattsburgh Make a Gift Who are you? Current Students Parents & Families School Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Community Jump to Footer Go back to the SUNY Plattsburgh Home Page About SUNY Plattsburgh Offices & Divisions Division of Administration & Finance Human Resource & Payroll Services Professional, Academic & Civil Service Jobs Internal Professional Promotion Plan Internal Professional Promotion Plan for Faculty & Staff Management and the UUP bargaining unit at SUNY Plattsburgh share the responsibility\n                              of maintaining a strong and motivated workforce. Our university's success depends\n                              on its employees, and this plan aims to recognize the value of those who dedicate\n                              their careers to SUNY Plattsburgh. We believe in fostering internal career development\n                              to boost employee morale and institutional success, offering current employees priority\n                              consideration for open positions. “Internal” promotions to vacant positions are provided for in the Memorandum of Understanding\n                           Relating to a System of Promotion and Certain Salary Increases for Professional Employees,\n                           III.E.(1). Additionally, this document clarifies the process outlined in the earlier\n                           Plattsburgh State Plan for Internal Professional Promotion (August 16, 1988).  For\n                           operational purposes and in addition to promotional opportunities, professional employees\n                           seeking lateral, non-promotional opportunities may also use this plan. UUP and SUNY Plattsburgh management recognize that certain situations will justify\n                           professional promotions being made to vacant positions that bypass the process described\n                           below.  For example, an assistant director or associate director may be the best person\n                           qualified to fill their department’s vacated director position, and in those instances,\n                           posting the position will not be necessary. These determinations will be made by management\n                           after weighing: (1) fairness to the professional employee by allowing an appropriate\n                           promotional opportunity, (2) campus affirmative action considerations, and (3) the\n                           greater needs of the campus. Furthermore, Article XII, Title C, section 6 of the SUNY Policies of the Board of\n                           Trustees authorizes the chief administrative officer (i.e., college president) to\n                           make personnel decisions: “Notwithstanding anything contained herein the chief administrative officer of a college\n                           may promote or recommend for promotion directly to the chancellor, or designee, any\n                           professional employee in the Professional Services Negotiating Unit at the chief administrative\n                           officer's college.” Nothing contained in this document shall serve to modify or lessen the rights and\n                           privileges assigned to campus management, United University Professions, or employees\n                           under the terms and conditions provided in the SUNY Policies of the Board of Trustees\n                           and the UUP/SUNY agreement. All UUP professional vacancies, including entry-level positions, will be covered by\n                           this plan. At the discretion of the president, after consultation with the affirmative action\n                           officer, this process may also be used for some positions designated as management/confidential.\n                           However, this process will not be used when searching for the positions of dean, vice\n                           president or provost. Specifically, it is the responsibility of the Human Resource and Payroll Services\n                           to ensure that the provisions of the UUP/NYS agreement are met regarding special consideration\n                           for retrenched university employees (Article 35). Posting of Approved Professional Vacancies At the outset of the process, notice of the vacancy will be posted internally for\n                                             a minimum period of 10 calendar days.  While internal postings will be made available\n                                             to all campus employees, it is the responsibility of HRS to ensure, within reason,\n                                             that internal postings are especially accessible to professional employees through\n                                             electronic, hard copy, and/or other means, and that the vacancy is announced to professional\n                                             employees as a promotional opportunity. Applications from campus employees, other than professional employees, received during\n                                             the internal posting period will not be accessible to reviewers until after decisions\n                                             have been made on all applications received from professional employees during the\n                                             internal posting period. Applications from internal applicants received after the internal posting period will\n                                             not be accessible to reviewers until after the internal review process is completed. The campus may opt to post the vacancy simultaneously in external sources. However,\n                                             any applications received from external applicants will not be accessible to reviewers\n                                             until after the internal review process is completed. Applicants for internal promotions under this process must have originally been selected\n                                             to a position on the campus as the result of a competitive search process.  Applications\n                                             will not be accepted from employees whose original campus appointment was as the result\n                                             of a search waiver. Disposition of Internal Applications Received During the Internal Posting Period References for internal applicants cannot be contacted without the applicants’ specific\n                                             approval. Applications from professional employees will be reviewed first to determine which\n                                             applicants are qualified or unqualified for the position. If reviewers recommend a\n                                             professional employee from this pool for promotion to the position, and that recommendation\n                                             is approved, then this process ends with the professional employee being promoted. If reviewers do not identify a professional employee for promotion to the position,\n                                             then applications from other (state) campus employees may be reviewed to determine\n                                             which applicants are qualified or unqualified for the position. If reviewers recommend\n                                             a campus employee from this second pool for appointment to the position, and that\n                                             recommendation is approved, then this process ends with the campus employee being\n                                             appointed. If reviewers do not identify an internal applicant for promotion or appointment to\n                                             this position, then applications from external applicants will be made available for\n                                             review.  Internal applicants previously judged qualified for the position but not\n                                             promoted or appointed during the internal review process will continue to be considered\n                                             following steps outlined for (external) searches. Internal applicants will be notified of the final disposition of their applications. April 24, 2009 Jobs — Recruitment Internal Professional Promotion Plan Recruitment & Online Recruiting System Contact Us Human Resource & Payroll Services 912 Kehoe Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-5062 Fax: 518-564-5060 [email protected] Office Hours Monday – Friday: 8 a.m. – 4 p.m. Jobs — Recruitment Internal Professional Promotion Plan Recruitment & Online Recruiting System Contact Us Human Resource & Payroll Services 912 Kehoe Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-5062 Fax: 518-564-5060 [email protected] Office Hours Monday – Friday: 8 a.m. – 4 p.m. Jump to Header Plattsburgh State University of New York Like us on Facebook. Find us on Instagram. Connect with us on Snapchat. Connect with us on LinkedIn. Login required. Watch us on YouTube. Virtual Tour Employment Emergency Info Find People Consumer Info Accessibility Title IX Feinberg Library Bookstore 101 Broad Street , Plattsburgh, NY 12901 • 518-564-2000 Copyright © 1996 – Privacy Policy Contact Us Last Updated 8/31/26 Back to top"
    },
    "https://www.plattsburgh.edu/about/offices-divisions/administration-finance/human-resources/jobs/ors.html": {
      "title": "Online Recruiting System (ORS)",
      "description": "Online Recruiting System (ORS) | SUNY Plattsburgh twitter brain business compass computer environment exit-site globe graph handshake health justice measure networking open-pdf pencil science trend video world arrow-right bars blogger caret-down caret-left caret-right caret-up close facebook gears home instagram linkedin logo play plus quote search snapchat-ghost tumblr virtual-tour women-network world-globe youtube-play logo-white Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Jump to Main Content Plattsburgh State University of New York Site Search Search Search SUNY Plattsburgh Visit Us Visit Apply Now Apply Request Info Info Academics Majors & Minors Online Programs Graduate Programs Microcredentials Schools & Departments Queensbury Campus Career Development Center Honors Program Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Academic Advising Feinberg Library Learning Center Study Abroad & Exchanges Technology Services Admissions First-Year Transfer Graduate International Readmission Educational Opportunity Program Non-Matriculated Students Registration Dates & Forms Apply Now Check Your Application Status Request More Information Visit & Event Options Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Scholarships, Loans & Grants Work Study & Student Jobs Apply for Aid Bill Paying & Refunds Net Price Calculator Graduate Student Aid Current Student Financial Aid Financial Services Forms PlattsLife Calendar of Events Activities & Getting Involved Campus Housing & Community Living Food & Dining Virtual Tour Our Location Visual & Performing Arts Campus TV & Radio Stations Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Health & Safety Career Development Center Student Support & Resources First Year Student Programs Commencement Sustainability Athletics Cardinal Athletics Recreational Sports & Programs Facilities Fitness Center Ticket Sales About Us President & Leadership Campus News Offices & Divisions Centers, Institutes & Clinics SUNY Plattsburgh at Queensbury Plattsburgh Next Mission, Vision & Values University Profile Consumer Information College Auxiliary Services Campus Facilities Directions & Campus Maps MyPlattsburgh Make a Gift Who are you? Current Students Parents & Families School Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Community Jump to Footer Go back to the SUNY Plattsburgh Home Page About SUNY Plattsburgh Offices & Divisions Division of Administration & Finance Human Resource & Payroll Services Professional, Academic & Civil Service Jobs Online Recruiting System (ORS) Online Recruiting System (ORS) Online Recruitment System (ORS) User’s Site [Login Required] Procedures Following are step-by-step instructions on how to navigate the ORS for those employees\n                           with the role of search chair, hiring authority, search committee member, as well\n                           as those administrative employees acting on behalf of one of the preceding roles.\n                           Please remember to consult the Recruitment Guide for details regarding recruitment on campus. Getting Started for Departments Once a position has been approved for recruitment, an Authorization to Recruit (ATR)\n                                          should be submitted in the ORS. An ATR should also be submitted for a Search Waiver\n                                          appointment. The ATR submission may be performed by a department chair, department\n                                          director, departmental secretary, or any other user with an approved “Department Authority”\n                                          role. Classified ATR Submission Procedure Unclassified ATR Submission Procedure The Recruitment Process for Search Chairs Once the position has been posted and applicants are being reviewed, the search chair\n                                          is responsible for updating the status of applicants and the search online, as well\n                                          as uploading supporting documentation. Step-by-Step Breakdown of the Recruitment Process (for Chairs Only) Adding a Search (ATR) to Your Watch List Helpful Tips for Narrowing the Pool Narrowing the Pool — Minimum Qualifications/Telephone Interviews Narrowing the Pool — Campus Interviews Submitting Finalists to the Hiring Authority Finalizing the Search Attaching Documents The Recruitment Process for Search Committee Members Once the position has been posted, search committee members are responsible for attending\n                                          and participating in meetings which will determine which candidates will move forward\n                                          in the search process. Procedure for reviewing candidates in the Online Recruiting System (ORS). The Hiring Process for Hiring Authorities Once the position has been offered and accepted, the hiring authority is usually responsible\n                                          for completing the hiring proposal. The procedure from completing a hire from the\n                                          Vita Bank may also be found below. Completing the Hiring Proposal — Unclassified Positions Completing the Hiring Proposal — Classified Positions Making a Hire from a Vita Bank Resources for Employees of the College Responsible for Recruitment Recruitment Guide Classification Assessment (for all vacant positions) Procedures for Using the Online Recruitment System Recruitment Process — Classified (Clerical/Maintenance/Service/Security) Recruitment Process — Unclassified (Professional/Academic) Title Descriptions (Classified Titles Only) Title Descriptions (Unclassified Titles Only) Jobs — Recruitment Internal Professional Promotion Plan Recruitment & Online Recruiting System Contact Us Human Resource & Payroll Services 912 Kehoe Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-5062 Fax: 518-564-5060 [email protected] Office Hours Monday – Friday: 8 a.m. – 4 p.m. Jobs — Recruitment Internal Professional Promotion Plan Recruitment & Online Recruiting System Contact Us Human Resource & Payroll Services 912 Kehoe Building 101 Broad Street Plattsburgh , NY 12901 Phone: 518-564-5062 Fax: 518-564-5060 [email protected] Office Hours Monday – Friday: 8 a.m. – 4 p.m. Jump to Header Plattsburgh State University of New York Like us on Facebook. Find us on Instagram. Connect with us on Snapchat. Connect with us on LinkedIn. Login required. Watch us on YouTube. Virtual Tour Employment Emergency Info Find People Consumer Info Accessibility Title IX Feinberg Library Bookstore 101 Broad Street , Plattsburgh, NY 12901 • 518-564-2000 Copyright © 1996 – Privacy Policy Contact Us Last Updated 8/31/26 Back to top"
    },
